 Leave it unset for normal training. When enabled, it exports every sequence from each exporting rank.

+## Exact snapshot rollout budgets
+
+Experiments that require every optimizer batch to use exactly one policy
+snapshot can enable the orchestrator's low-throughput strict mode:
+
+```toml
+[orchestrator]
+max_off_policy_steps = 0
+strict_snapshot_batches = true
+train_groups_per_policy = 1
+
+[weight_broadcast]
+type = "filesystem"
+```
+
+`train_groups_per_policy` is the number of complete environment groups needed
+to fill one optimizer batch. Strict mode stops opening groups after that
+number, waits until the trainer's filesystem checkpoint has been fully applied
+to inference, runs any evaluation scheduled for that snapshot to completion,
+and only then opens the next training cohort. Use it for exact call accounting
+and snapshot-aligned evaluation, not throughput-oriented production runs. The
+config validator rejects nonzero `max_off_policy_steps` and non-filesystem
+weight broadcast in this mode.
+
 ## Key files

 - `packages/prime-rl-configs/src/prime_rl/` — config classes under `configs/`; `utils/config.py` re-exports `BaseConfig` and `cli`
